# S10.2D-R1 Community preflight command diagnosis — 2026-09-05

## Safe result

The read-only BotFather capability check completed green. The following
temporary target-archive verification stopped before provider verification
because the manually composed archive extraction command named a nonexistent
executable. `set -e` stopped immediately and the exact `mktemp` directory had
an EXIT cleanup trap. No repository, configuration, service, database,
Telegram or public state was changed.

## Root cause and bounded correction

This was a command transcription error, not a product or infrastructure
failure. The correction is to reuse the already reviewed sequence from
`target_community_verify`: create one exact `/run` scratch directory, stream
the exact target Git archive into standard `tar -x -C`, execute the official
read-only Community verifier, and delete only that scratch directory through
the existing `find "$scratch" -depth -delete` pattern.

No deployment, retry or new architecture is authorized by this diagnosis.
